# Review: SpotlightPlugin

The code matches the spec closely. `SpotlightOperationHandlerSet` intercepts `UpdateDialog`, `Open`,
`SwitchWorkspace` and `Close` exactly as described, with the 100 ms `DISMISS_DEBOUNCE_MS`, and
registers no-op handlers for the eight listed layout operations. `SpotlightLayout` renders the
commands dialog in a non-modal `Dialog.Root`, resets state on focus and focuses the search input.
`SpotlightDismiss` hides the window on focus loss and Escape. The `State` module publishes the
spotlight `Layout` atom.

The gap is tests. The only test, `plugin.test.ts`, checks that the `State`, `SpotlightDismiss` and
`OperationHandler` modules activate; no test runs a handler, the dismiss listeners or the layout.
Every behaviour is therefore `untested`, and no acceptance scenario has automation. All handlers
call Tauri APIs, so a test would need stubs for `@tauri-apps/api`. The QA test is human-only and
marked `blocked` in the spec.

